      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Positivity converts an analytic identity into inequalities without cancellation loss. Separating a main range from the tail makes the proof modular: coefficient positivity handles the main comparison, while a crude lower bound for L(1) and auxiliary estimates make the tail controllable.",
