    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_e200ebd87f36a7ac4fed015f24cf8882b1563e3afd44364217acdecb4ddb38dd",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Lemma 3 places one logarithmically weighted auxiliary-coefficient sum in correspondence with an expression involving L-function values, a derivative contribution, and controlled errors; the following elementary real-analysis lemma supplies two summation relations declared for its derivation. The conceptual gain is a single translation point between coefficient data and local analytic data, so later work can reason through either representation. At this statement-only stage nothing establishes positivity, behavior at zeros, or a contradiction, and the translation loses reliability at the level of exact weights, coefficients, error terms, and parameter ranges because the formulas are OCR-damaged. The real nonprincipal character assumption and the stated parameter restrictions remain part of the unresolved proof obligation.",
