    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_06cd3b4d262393e18b53b3a1b597b491723c1c8aa8d6170498e567cd165a75e8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Lemma 3 translates a logarithmically weighted auxiliary-coefficient sum into L-function values, a derivative term, and errors. Its derivation splits at a tunable cutoff, evaluates the structured pieces by elementary summation, and controls weighted tails by Pólya-Vinogradov partial-sum cancellation plus Abel's inequality. A forbidden two-zero or multiple-zero configuration then supplies an intermediate point with nonpositive L-value and vanishing derivative, making the analytic upper estimate quantitatively incompatible with the positive coefficient-side lower bound. The closing remark abstracts the interface to real-valued completely multiplicative functions with bounded values and the required partial-sum control.",
